{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1531411-ancient-clans-beyond-the-roman-camarilla-also-homebrew","id":1531411,"title":"Ancient Clans Beyond The Roman Camarilla (Also Homebrew)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-23T23:02:47-08:00","id":1531411,"title":"Ancient Clans Beyond The Roman Camarilla (Also Homebrew)","content":"Besides the Grettir, Akhud and Baali in Requiem For Rome 2e. Are there other clans beyond the five that once existed until they became seemingly extinct in other parts of the globe? Was wondering if there was once clans in Asia that were the Ventrue/Julii analogues but I guess the Daeva may already fill the niche even without a clan that fills the same purpose.<br /> <br /> My idea so far is that there was once a clan in India who are called the Asuras. They were like rivals to the Daeva who are also native to the area (made them rivals due to mythological reasons). Due to their seemingly demonic nature since I imagine they have protean amalgams that are similar to demon shintai from KOTE, the daeva may have rallied other clans such as nosferatu, mekhet and gangrel into a holy war against the clan. The asuras may have been driven extinct, but some kindred may have diablerized them resulting in bloodlines such as Amara Havana and Rakshasa (For the Amara Havana, one of their origin stories tell that they were the result of the mixing of Kali and the demon Raktabija could be interpreted that they were from Daeva who diablerized Asura during the holy war). Some of the Asuras may have survived and even joined the VII out of vengeance. The Asuras may also be related to the onis and may have even resulted in myths about them, but they were onis in one of the Dark Eras books but they can be explained as a non-embracing offshoot that separated from the Asuras before they evolved into kindred.<br /> <br /> So far my ideas for the Asuras is this.<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Demon Kings<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Protean, Animalism, Vigor. (Although may probably make it Protean, Majesty and Vigor to imply they are related to the Daeva thanks to a common ancestor)<br /> <br /> <b>Bane: </b>Maybe something similar to a Wraith The Oblivion shadow? I'm new to Requiem so I'm not good at the mechanics yet.<br /> <br /> I also have ideas for a Julii/Ventrue analogue in ancient China that may be the result of an apocryphal Taoist immortal cursed by the other immortals and the gods. But the Daeva could still fill the niche as they might use the myth of Nuwa to legitimize their role as rulers.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25313-raziel","name":"Raziel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-24T01:15:20-08:00","id":1531415,"title":"","content":"There are a good few more. The following index lists Clans from official material, that have known Disciplines:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://codexofdarkness.com/wiki/Clans_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Codex of Darkness</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-24T05:26:06-08:00","id":1531420,"title":"","content":"While there are examples for non Roman Clans during that time period, the question is probably whether or not those are Clans who make sense as coming in interaction with Rome- for example, the fact that the Cecenya are likely active in Mesoamerica does not really help as it is unlikely that they would come in contact with Rome. I have made my own African Clan called the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JCWQcSiqHtmIeEruJHwPp3Btnm15adVfHJA9GK2roAU/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">Mumvuri</a> as part of a community project which have came from the &quot;Land of Punt&quot;, so they might be relevant for your question. The Amari are likely also relevant (and the Mikhailli, if you see them as a separate Clan).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-24T06:10:26-08:00","id":1531423,"title":"","content":"Requiem for Rome 2 has the Baali who are not Roman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-24T06:26:46-08:00","id":1531424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1531411-ancient-clans-beyond-the-roman-camarilla-also-homebrew?p=1531420#post1531420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While there are examples for non Roman Clans during that time period, the question is probably whether or not those are Clans who make sense as coming in interaction with Rome- for example, the fact that the Cecenya are likely active in Mesoamerica does not really help as it is unlikely that they would come in contact with Rome. I have made my own African Clan called the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JCWQcSiqHtmIeEruJHwPp3Btnm15adVfHJA9GK2roAU/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">Mumvuri</a> as part of a community project which have came from the &quot;Land of Punt&quot;, so they might be relevant for your question. The Amari are likely also relevant (and the Mikhailli, if you see them as a separate Clan).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, not all clans at that time had contact with the Propinqui of Rome. <br /> <br /> Although I mostly meant historical lost clans in general not just near Rome or even the same time period, so your homebrew doc can still work.<br /> <br /> So far, my ideas for Asia in ancient times is that the Jiang Shi still aren't kindred yet but slowly gained traits over time thanks to contact. Daeva are both in the Fertile Crescent and the Indian subcontinent since I imagine they existed before the split between Indo-European cultures. <br /> <br /> Although I remember they aren't a lost clan, since their numbers are just low but in my headcanon, they became true kindred and lost that weakness when it comes to embracing new Jiang Shi in the modern times.<br /> <br /> May also try to make the Penanggalan a true clan but that should be a separate post on it's own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25313-raziel","name":"Raziel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T08:04:08-08:00","id":1531471,"title":"","content":"Didn't <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Night_Horrors:_Spilled_Blood#Lost_/_Minor_Clans\" target=\"_blank\">Spilled Blood</a> have a few clans too? Definitely worth checking out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T00:43:10-08:00","id":1531496,"title":"","content":"The Uttuku and Lilitu are also mentioned as lot Clans, even though they have never gotten any mechanics","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T22:20:22-08:00","id":1531996,"title":"","content":"I also have another idea for a historical lost clan which is a a Ventrue/Julii analog called the Yuhuang or the False Xian. They believe they are from an apocryphal Taoist immortal cursed by the heavens. Their bane is similar to a She Who Lives In Her Name urge from Exalted and their discipline set would be Dominate, Auspex but I can't think of a good third discipline for them. Maybe Animalism or Obfuscate? I may give them different reasons for their extinction unlike the Julii or Baali from VTR, but I may make some implications that some lived and got absorbed where the survivors became a Ventrue bloodline. They also know a type of sorcery based on Taoism but unlike the False Xian, the art survived thanks to other kindred practitioners.<br /> <br /> I may also discuss the Penanggalan and Aswang from Night Horrors: Wicked Dead as a clan called the Langsuir as they slowly became kindred in the modern nights but will make it a separate post in this forum alongside the Jiang Shi.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25313-raziel","name":"Raziel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T17:05:13-08:00","id":1532066,"title":"","content":"I've written up number of ancient clans to varying degrees, though not too many specific to the Camarilla era. The only one I remember writing up was a psuedo-cousin of the Gangrel called the Baersarks, a clan from Germania that had a vendetta against the Legio Mortuum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T04:34:49-08:00","id":1532077,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1686_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1686\" data-vbnamecard=\"1686\">Korogra</a> could you please share said ancient clans? Or at least provide links to them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T12:43:20-08:00","id":1532100,"title":"","content":"Minor aside, but also bringing up some bloodlines of questionable origins:<br /> <br /> - <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Rakshasa_(VTR)\" target=\"_blank\">Rakshasa</a>, who in a certain version of their origins, began as <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Larvae_(Zero_Blood_Potency)\" target=\"_blank\">hungry corpses</a> uplifted into kindred condition by the civilizing/taming efforts of an undead brahmin.<br /> - <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vedma\" target=\"_blank\">Vedma</a>, a bloodline of eastern european witches among whom some members claim to predate the Gangrel in lineage.<br /> - <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Annunaku\" target=\"_blank\">Annunaku</a>, while better known as Gangrel landlords, according to some rumors, cross the lines into Ventrue and may predate not only the Invictus, but the Camarilla itself.<br /> - <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gorgon_(VTR)\" target=\"_blank\">Gorgons</a>, though more associated with the Mediterranean than Mesopotamia or the Middle East, also tell a similar tale of links to lost gods &amp; monsters and predating covenants present and past.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are probably a number of others i forget, but 4 is a good start i guess. Will add some more if i remember anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-06-2024, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T16:10:11-08:00","id":1532123,"title":"","content":"Had added the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cihuateteo\" target=\"_blank\">Cihuateteo</a> to the list, but then while reading the wiki text realized that official materials <b>never </b>really adressed any possible relation between either bloodline or the witches from Wicked Dead.<br /> <br /> A link through service to their gods, with dead Cihuateteo spontaneously on the form closer to the deity they were more beholden to, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tezcatlipoca\" target=\"_blank\">Jaguar</a> (Gangrel) &amp; the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tlaz%C5%8Dlte%C5%8Dtl\" target=\"_blank\">Whore</a> (Daeva), blurring the lines between clan, bloodline and other, while based on a common mythology &amp; fluff, was 100% me confusing homebrew from chronicles long past with actual canon, my bad. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For an extra bonus, the chapter on Ars Speculorum in Mythologies would also mention in passing the possibility of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ars_Speculorum\" target=\"_blank\">Red Jack</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Children_of_the_Thorns\" target=\"_blank\">Bloody Mary</a> being newer forms of both deities, before either version of the Cihuateteo was a thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Beside this &quot;alternative&quot; take on the Cihuateteo, i did sketch out a few other clans from mixing and matching from book bits and other stuff.<br /> <br /> An east asian clan, where i mixed <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Formosae\" target=\"_blank\">Formosae</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Galloi\" target=\"_blank\">Galloi </a>&amp; <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Aswang\" target=\"_blank\">Aswang</a> (though more precisely an all-female &quot;early edition&quot; variant from the Antagonists bluebook) under a &quot;beauty hiding atrocity&quot; theme, based on Taiwan (because Formosa, duh <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) and worshipping a cthonic version of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doumu\" target=\"_blank\">Doumu</a> in place of Cybele. Though i'll be the first to admit i was just improvising from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Izanami\" target=\"_blank\">Izanami </a>more than anything. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Another early play at making a clan was something of a weird revenge of mine over a player's insistence of having his Khabit's sire be an ancient harkening to the Roman Empire when my original intent was to keep the scale and timespan mostly within the low hundreds/age of sail, at least to start.<br /> <br /> &quot;So he wants a sire from Rome? Good for him, because i'll make a Khaibit Victrix, betrayer of the Senex, doom of the Julii, out of her! &quot;<br /> <br /> And well, from me playing with the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Khaibit\" target=\"_blank\">Khaibit</a>'s 1e discipline set (as close to Daeva as Mekhet), redoing Victrix's backstory with some <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Siege_of_Numantia\" target=\"_blank\">decidedly iberian</a> twists and themes and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dis_(Divine_Comedy)\" target=\"_blank\">some </a>extras and <a href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Dispater\" target=\"_blank\">deviations</a> for the intervening <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Belial&#39;s_Brood\" target=\"_blank\">c</a>enturies, would come to be the Numantine clan, as a sort of shadowy undercurrent moving between Mekhet, Daeva, Khaibit, Circle of Crone, Belial's Brood and VII perhaps, but not quite the face of either or how one would expect them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_